# Normalize line endings so a checkout is byte-identical no matter what the
# clone's core.autocrlf is set to.
#
# Why this exists: on 2026-10-15 a restore proof cloned this vault onto a
# machine with the Git for Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) and every text
# file came back with CRLF endings, so CORE.md read 5306 bytes on disk against
# 5191 in the live vault. The blob hashes matched, so nothing was lost -- but
# anything that counts or hashes on-disk bytes (token budgeting, byte-identical
# restore checks) would then behave differently after a restore than it does in
# the live vault. Pinning eol makes the restore deterministic.
#
# LF is the pin, not CRLF: it matches what the live vault already uses and what
# the object store already holds for most files.
*.md      text eol=lf
*.ps1     text eol=lf
*.mjs     text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must never be checked out with CRLF: bash cannot run them.
*.sh      text eol=lf
